  "summary": "Overnight, US Treasury yields moved lower with the 10-year at 4.84% and the 2-year at 4.46% as traders positioned for the jobs release; SOFR is 3.94% and futures imply a gradual rise toward the mid-4.3% area by late 2027. Equities stayed firm with the S&P 500 at 7688.62 and Nasdaq at 24315, while gold held 4113.5 after the US congressional shift initially pressured the dollar and lifted bullion. The Bank of England raised Bank Rate to 4.0%, its first increase since the Iran war began, and warned inflation could approach 5%. Canada and the Bank of Canada renewed their inflation-targeting framework. Stress around AI-related leverage intensified, with SoftBank credit risk at a four-year high and banks reportedly marketing data-center loans. The period ahead turns on US employment data, ECB inputs toward the December meeting, and whether tech-financing strains broaden.",
